_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 7
---
order: 7
---
short_label: XIII.7
---
sections:

#### prop_section ####
kind: proposition
----
statement: If three angles of an equilateral pentagon, taken either in order or not in order, are equal, then the pentagon is equiangular.
----
proof:

First, let three angles {A|angA}, {B|angB}, and {C|angC} taken in order in the equilateral pentagon {ABCDE|pentT} be equal to one another.

I say that the pentagon {ABCDE|pentT} is equiangular.

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="265" height="240" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="XIII.7 diagram" src="propXIII7.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    // Two cases on one figure. The first (angles A, B, C equal) uses AC, BE
    // and FD; the second (angles A, C, D equal) uses BE and BD, so its
    // slides drop AC, FD and F and keep BE, which the first case joined.
    //
    // Joyce's element "FC" is the line from F to D (connect F,D): the prose
    // calls it FD and reaches it as {FD|FC}. The segment FC of AC that the
    // remainder step names is segFC, reached as {FC|segFC}.
    //
    // Joyce's pentagon ABCDE keeps its random face and is never highlighted
    // (a highlighted face is raised over the markers, #140); "the pentagon
    // ABCDE" reaches pentT, a faceless twin. Everything else added is
    // transparent: the five sides, the segments AF, BF, segFC, FE, and the
    // triangles ABC, ABE, BCD (explicit ;0 faces).
    //
    // Angle markers: whole angles purple at 30, the parts at 18 so the two
    // parts at one vertex lie side by side inside the whole. Equal parts
    // share a colour: BCA = BEA (= AEB = CDB) blue, ABE = CAB green,
    // FCD = FED (= BED = BDE) orange. No angle is treated as right.
    //
    // Draggables (checked against the bundle): A and B, free — the given
    // pentagon's side, standing from slide 1. C, D, E, F are derived and
    // listed per slide; nothing to defer.
    var GIVEN = ["ABCDE","pentT","A","B","C","D","E","AB","BC","CD","DE","EA"];
    var WHOLE = ["angA","angB","angC","angD","angE"];
    var HYP   = GIVEN.concat(["angA","angB","angC"]);
    var JOIN  = HYP.concat(["AC","BE","F","FC","AF","BF","segFC","FE","ABC","ABE"]);
    var BASE  = JOIN.concat(["angBCA","angBEA"]);
    var OPP   = BASE.concat(["angABE","angCAB"]);
    var FCD   = OPP.concat(["angFCD","angBED"]);
    var AED   = FCD.concat(["angE"]);
    var ALL   = AED.concat(["angD"]);
    var NEXT  = GIVEN.concat(["BE"]);
    var HYP2  = NEXT.concat(["angA","angC","angD"]);
    var JOIN2 = HYP2.concat(["BD","ABE","BCD"]);
    var BASE2 = JOIN2.concat(["angBEA","angCDB"]);
    var ISO2  = BASE2.concat(["angBED","angBDE"]);
    var AED2  = ISO2.concat(["angE"]);
    var ALL2  = AED2.concat(["angB"]);
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "XIII.7",
        elements: [
            "A;point;free;130,40",
            "B;point;free;39,106",
            "ABCDE;polygon;regularPolygon;A,B,5;0;0;black;random",
            "C;point;vertex;ABCDE,3",
            "D;point;vertex;ABCDE,4",
            "E;point;vertex;ABCDE,5",
            "AC;line;connect;A,C",
            "BE;line;connect;B,E",
            "F;point;intersection;AC,BE",
            "FC;line;connect;F,D",
            "BD;line;connect;B,D",
            // Faceless twin of the pentagon (see above).
            "pentT;polygon;regularPolygon;A,B,5;0;0;0;0",
            // Transparent highlight targets.
            "AB;line;connect;A,B;0;0;0",
            "BC;line;connect;B,C;0;0;0",
            "CD;line;connect;C,D;0;0;0",
            "DE;line;connect;D,E;0;0;0",
            "EA;line;connect;E,A;0;0;0",
            "AF;line;connect;A,F;0;0;0",
            "BF;line;connect;B,F;0;0;0",
            "segFC;line;connect;F,C;0;0;0",
            "FE;line;connect;F,E;0;0;0",
            "ABC;polygon;triangle;A,B,C;0;0;0;0",
            "ABE;polygon;triangle;A,B,E;0;0;0;0",
            "BCD;polygon;triangle;B,C,D;0;0;0;0",
            // Angle markers.
            "angA;sector;angleMarker;A,B,E,30;0;0;7a4fa3;cdb8e6",
            "angB;sector;angleMarker;B,A,C,30;0;0;7a4fa3;cdb8e6",
            "angC;sector;angleMarker;C,B,D,30;0;0;7a4fa3;cdb8e6",
            "angD;sector;angleMarker;D,C,E,30;0;0;7a4fa3;cdb8e6",
            "angE;sector;angleMarker;E,D,A,30;0;0;7a4fa3;cdb8e6",
            "angBCA;sector;angleMarker;C,B,A,18;0;0;3b6ea5;9ec5e8",
            "angBEA;sector;angleMarker;E,B,A,18;0;0;3b6ea5;9ec5e8",
            "angCDB;sector;angleMarker;D,C,B,18;0;0;3b6ea5;9ec5e8",
            "angABE;sector;angleMarker;B,A,E,18;0;0;3f8e4f;a8dbb0",
            "angCAB;sector;angleMarker;A,C,B,18;0;0;3f8e4f;a8dbb0",
            "angFCD;sector;angleMarker;C,A,D,18;0;0;c06a1b;f3c590",
            "angBED;sector;angleMarker;E,B,D,18;0;0;c06a1b;f3c590",
            "angBDE;sector;angleMarker;D,B,E,18;0;0;c06a1b;f3c590"
        ],
        aliases: { "CB": "BC", "BA": "AB", "AE": "EA", "ED": "DE", "DC": "CD",
                   "EB": "BE", "CA": "AC", "DB": "BD", "FB": "BF", "EF": "FE" },
        slides: [
            { text: "“If three angles of an equilateral pentagon, taken either in order or not in order, are equal,”",
              visible: GIVEN,
              highlighted: ["pentT"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "XIII.7" }] },
            { text: "“then the pentagon is equiangular.”",
              visible: GIVEN.concat(WHOLE),
              highlighted: WHOLE,
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "angA", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angB", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angC", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angD", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angE", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "First, let three angles {A|angA}, {B|angB}, and {C|angC} taken in order in the equilateral pentagon {ABCDE|pentT} be equal to one another.",
              visible: HYP,
              highlighted: ["angA","angB","angC"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "angA", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angB", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angC", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "I say that the pentagon {ABCDE|pentT} is equiangular.",
              visible: HYP,
              highlighted: ["pentT"] },
            { text: "Join {AC}, {BE}, and {FD|FC}.",
              visible: JOIN,
              highlighted: ["AC","BE","FC"],
              transition: { mode: "cascade", animations: [
                  { elem: "AC", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "BE", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect },
                  { elem: "F",  name: geomlib.A.Point.appear },
                  { elem: "FC", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.Post.1" }] },
            { text: "Now, since the two sides {CB} and {BA} equal the two sides {BA} and {AE} respectively,",
              visible: JOIN,
              highlighted: ["BC","AB","EA"] },
            { text: "and the angle {CBA|angB} equals the angle {BAE|angA},",
              visible: JOIN,
              highlighted: ["angB","angA"] },
            { text: "therefore the base {AC} equals the base {BE}, the triangle {ABC} equals the triangle {ABE},",
              visible: JOIN,
              highlighted: ["AC","BE","ABC","ABE"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "ABC", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outline },
                  { elem: "ABE", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outline } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "two sides and the included angle", ref: "I.4" }] },
            { text: "and the remaining angles equal the remaining angles, namely those opposite the equal sides,",
              visible: JOIN,
              highlighted: ["ABC","ABE"] },
            { text: "that is, the angle {BCA|angBCA} equals the angle {BEA|angBEA},",
              visible: BASE,
              highlighted: ["angBCA","angBEA"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "angBCA", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angBEA", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "and the angle {ABE|angABE} equals the angle {CAB|angCAB}.",
              visible: OPP,
              highlighted: ["angABE","angCAB"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "angABE", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angCAB", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "Hence the side {AF} also equals the side {BF}.",
              visible: OPP,
              highlighted: ["AF","BF"],
              justifications: [{ claim: "angle FAB = angle FBA", ref: "I.6" }] },
            { text: "But the whole {AC} equals the whole {BE},",
              visible: OPP,
              highlighted: ["AC","BE"] },
            { text: "therefore the remainder {FC|segFC} equals the remainder {FE}.",
              visible: OPP,
              highlighted: ["segFC","FE"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "C.N.3" }] },
            { text: "But {CD} also equals {DE}.",
              visible: OPP,
              highlighted: ["CD","DE"] },
            { text: "Therefore the two sides {FC|segFC} and {CD} equal the two sides {FE} and {ED},",
              visible: OPP,
              highlighted: ["segFC","CD","FE","DE"] },
            { text: "and the base {FD|FC} is common to them,",
              visible: OPP,
              highlighted: ["FC"] },
            { text: "therefore the angle {FCD|angFCD} equals the angle {FED|angBED}.",
              visible: FCD,
              highlighted: ["angFCD","angBED"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "angFCD", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angBED", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "three sides equal", ref: "I.8" }] },
            { text: "But the angle {BCA|angBCA} was also proved equal to the angle {AEB|angBEA},",
              visible: FCD,
              highlighted: ["angBCA","angBEA"] },
            { text: "therefore the whole angle {BCD|angC} equals the whole angle {AED|angE}.",
              visible: AED,
              highlighted: ["angC","angE"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "angE", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "C.N.2" }] },
            { text: "And, by hypothesis, the angle {BCD|angC} equals the angles at {A|angA} and {B|angB},",
              visible: AED,
              highlighted: ["angC","angA","angB"] },
            { text: "therefore the angle {AED|angE} also equals the angles at {A|angA} and {B|angB}.",
              visible: AED,
              highlighted: ["angE","angA","angB"] },
            { text: "Similarly we can prove that the angle {CDE|angD} also equals the angles at {A|angA}, {B|angB}, and {C|angC}.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["angD","angA","angB","angC"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "angD", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "Therefore the pentagon {ABCDE|pentT} is equiangular.",
              visible: ALL,
              highlighted: ["pentT"].concat(WHOLE) },
            { text: "Next, let the given equal angles not be angles taken in order,",
              visible: NEXT,
              highlighted: ["pentT"] },
            { text: "but let the angles at the points {A|angA}, {C|angC}, and {D|angD} be equal.",
              visible: HYP2,
              highlighted: ["angA","angC","angD"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "angA", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angC", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angD", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "I say that in this case too the pentagon {ABCDE|pentT} is equiangular.",
              visible: HYP2,
              highlighted: ["pentT"] },
            { text: "Join {BD}.",
              visible: JOIN2,
              highlighted: ["BD"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "BD", name: geomlib.A.Line.straightEdgeConnect } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.Post.1" }] },
            { text: "Then, since the two sides {BA} and {AE} equal the two sides {BC} and {CD}, and they contain equal angles,",
              visible: JOIN2,
              highlighted: ["AB","EA","BC","CD","angA","angC"] },
            { text: "therefore the base {BE} equals the base {BD}, the triangle {ABE} equals the triangle {BCD},",
              visible: JOIN2,
              highlighted: ["BE","BD","ABE","BCD"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "ABE", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outline },
                  { elem: "BCD", name: geomlib.A.Polygon.outline } ] },
              justifications: [{ claim: "two sides and the included angle", ref: "I.4" }] },
            { text: "and the remaining angles equal the remaining angles, namely those opposite the equal sides.",
              visible: JOIN2,
              highlighted: ["ABE","BCD"] },
            { text: "Therefore the angle {AEB|angBEA} equals the angle {CDB|angCDB}.",
              visible: BASE2,
              highlighted: ["angBEA","angCDB"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "angBEA", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angCDB", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "But the angle {BED|angBED} also equals the angle {BDE|angBDE},",
              visible: ISO2,
              highlighted: ["angBED","angBDE"],
              transition: { mode: "parallel", animations: [
                  { elem: "angBED", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep },
                  { elem: "angBDE", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "since the side {BE} equals the side {BD}.",
              visible: ISO2,
              highlighted: ["BE","BD"],
              justifications: [{ ref: "I.5" }] },
            { text: "Therefore the whole angle {AED|angE} equals the whole angle {CDE|angD}.",
              visible: AED2,
              highlighted: ["angE","angD"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "angE", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] },
              justifications: [{ ref: "C.N.2" }] },
            { text: "But the angle {CDE|angD} is, by hypothesis, equal to the angles at {A|angA} and {C|angC},",
              visible: AED2,
              highlighted: ["angD","angA","angC"] },
            { text: "therefore the angle {AED|angE} also equals the angles at {A|angA} and {C|angC}.",
              visible: AED2,
              highlighted: ["angE","angA","angC"] },
            { text: "For the same reason the angle {ABC|angB} also equals the angles at {A|angA}, {C|angC}, and {D|angD}.",
              visible: ALL2,
              highlighted: ["angB","angA","angC","angD"],
              transition: { animations: [
                  { elem: "angB", name: geomlib.A.Sector.sweep } ] } },
            { text: "Therefore the pentagon {ABCDE|pentT} is equiangular.",
              visible: ALL2,
              highlighted: ["pentT"].concat(WHOLE) },
            { text: "Therefore, if three angles of an equilateral pentagon, taken either in order or not in order, are equal,",
              visible: GIVEN.concat(WHOLE),
              highlighted: ["pentT"] },
            { text: "then the pentagon is equiangular.",
              visible: GIVEN.concat(WHOLE),
              highlighted: WHOLE,
              justifications: [{ ref: "Q.E.D." }] }
        ],
        resolveJustification: function(ref) {
            if (ref === "XIII.7") return "#prop";
            return (window.eucrefs && window.eucrefs[ref]) || null;
        }
    });

    // Per-page citation lookup for the slideshow's resolveJustification.
    window.eucrefs = (window.eucrefs || {});
    Object.assign(window.eucrefs, {
        "I.Post.1": "/elements/books/bookI/postulates/post1/",
        "C.N.2":    "/elements/books/bookI/commonnotions/cn2/",
        "C.N.3":    "/elements/books/bookI/commonnotions/cn3/",
        "I.4":      "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI4/",
        "I.5":      "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI5/",
        "I.6":      "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI6/",
        "I.8":      "/elements/books/bookI/propositions/propI8/"
    });
</script>
</figure>

Join {AC}, {BE}, and {FD|FC}.

Now, since the two sides {CB} and {BA} equal the two sides {BA} and {AE} respectively, and the angle {CBA|angB} equals the angle {BAE|angA}, therefore the base {AC} equals the base {BE}, the triangle {ABC} equals the triangle {ABE}, and the remaining angles equal the remaining angles, namely those opposite the equal sides, that is, the angle {BCA|angBCA} equals the angle {BEA|angBEA}, and the angle {ABE|angABE} equals the angle {CAB|angCAB}. [!just I.4]

Hence the side {AF} also equals the side {BF}. [!just I.6]

But the whole {AC} equals the whole {BE}, therefore the remainder {FC|segFC} equals the remainder {FE}. But {CD} also equals {DE}. Therefore the two sides {FC|segFC} and {CD} equal the two sides {FE} and {ED}, and the base {FD|FC} is common to them, therefore the angle {FCD|angFCD} equals the angle {FED|angBED}. [!just I.8]

But the angle {BCA|angBCA} was also proved equal to the angle {AEB|angBEA}, therefore the whole angle {BCD|angC} equals the whole angle {AED|angE}. And, by hypothesis, the angle {BCD|angC} equals the angles at {A|angA} and {B|angB}, therefore the angle {AED|angE} also equals the angles at {A|angA} and {B|angB}. Similarly we can prove that the angle {CDE|angD} also equals the angles at {A|angA}, {B|angB}, and {C|angC}. Therefore the pentagon {ABCDE|pentT} is equiangular.

<hr width="40%">

Next, let the given equal angles not be angles taken in order, but let the angles at the points {A|angA}, {C|angC}, and {D|angD} be equal.

I say that in this case too the pentagon {ABCDE|pentT} is equiangular.

Join {BD}.

Then, since the two sides {BA} and {AE} equal the two sides {BC} and {CD}, and they contain equal angles, therefore the base {BE} equals the base {BD}, the triangle {ABE} equals the triangle {BCD}, and the remaining angles equal the remaining angles, namely those opposite the equal sides. Therefore the angle {AEB|angBEA} equals the angle {CDB|angCDB}. [!just I.4]

But the angle {BED|angBED} also equals the angle {BDE|angBDE}, since the side {BE} equals the side {BD}. [!just I.5]

Therefore the whole angle {AED|angE} equals the whole angle {CDE|angD}.

But the angle {CDE|angD} is, by hypothesis, equal to the angles at {A|angA} and {C|angC}, therefore the angle {AED|angE} also equals the angles at {A|angA} and {C|angC}.

For the same reason the angle {ABC|angB} also equals the angles at {A|angA}, {C|angC}, and {D|angD}. Therefore the pentagon {ABCDE|pentT} is equiangular.

Therefore, *if three angles of an equilateral pentagon, taken either in order or not in order, are equal, then the pentagon is equiangular.*

<div class="qed">Q.E.D.</div>
----
guide:

#### Use of this proposition

This proposition is needed in @XIII.17 to show that the dodecahedron constructed there has equiangular pentagons as faces.
